WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.860
- [Narrator] Salami slicing tactics.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.650
It's not a method for cutting deli meats.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.120
It's a military strategy

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.030
that China has used in
the South China Sea.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.302
This salami represents the sea.

00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:13.830
Each slice is a portion of the region

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.900
that China has claimed over decades,

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.860
often angering its neighbors
who hold competing claims.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.740
And the US missed the moment to intervene,

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.830
in part because it was
focused on working with China

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:29.850
to mediate other global issues
in North Korea and Iran.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.863
In that time, China
occupied various coral reefs

00:00:32.863 --> 00:00:36.840
and in some cases, turned
them into artificial islands.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.200
Today it controls 27
outposts across the sea,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.463
largely in disputed areas,

00:00:42.463 --> 00:00:45.720
which is why this mostly chopped up salami

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.305
represents the state of the sea

00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:49.980
now that the US has taken
a more critical stance

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.450
against China.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.123
So what is it doing to counter Beijing?

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.650
The South China Sea is
central to the Indo-Pacific

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.070
where 60% of the world's population lives.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.200
Trillions of dollars worth of trade

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.060
passes through the sea each year.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.890
According to the China Power Project

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.980
by the Center for Strategic
and International Studies,

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:14.400
1/3 of all global trade transits the sea,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.680
making many countries
economically dependent

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.060
on the region.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.920
It's critical to the US economy

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.680
because America imports around 90%

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.620
of its advanced microchips from Taiwan.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.717
And roughly 14% of American maritime trade

00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:31.830
transited the sea in 2016.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:34.680
But in that same year, over 64%

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.267
of China's maritime trade passed through.

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.273
$874 billion.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.350
China is the largest exporter
of goods in the region.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.750
And having control over more of the sea

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.510
would potentially give
the PRC a lot of power

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:52.560
over the economies of the US
and all of China's neighbors.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.420
- It is because national security

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.140
is no longer simply about
territorial defense.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.220
Economic security is national security

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.110
- [Narrator] And that's why
the disputes in the region

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:07.560
often focus on one big jargony term,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.230
exclusive economic zones.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.310
EEZs are areas in the sea
where country has jurisdiction

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.840
over the resources.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.837
They generally extend
around 200 nautical miles.

00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:21.990
(crowd chattering)

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.610
And because countries like Vietnam

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.970
and the Philippines rely
on access to these areas,

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.220
China's encroachment has posed a problem

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.040
for their security and economies.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.440
- So you hear the fishermen complaining

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.450
of China's aggressive action

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.690
and denying them the ability to fish

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:44.370
in our own exclusive economic
zone, in our own waters.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.500
- [Narrator] China says
it has historical claims

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.840
to almost the entire South China Sea

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.590
based on a map from 1947
that illustrates dashes

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.720
cutting through the majority of the sea.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.900
Fittingly, it's called the nine-dash line,

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.390
but that line cuts through EEZ claims

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.310
for five other countries.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.920
To try and solidify its claim to the sea,

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.040
China has been incrementally
occupying various islands

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.960
to slowly change the status
quo, aka salami slicing.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.270
It began this process in the 1970s

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:18.990
when it took control of the
Paracel Islands from Vietnam.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:22.440
In 1995, China occupied Mischief Reef

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:25.470
which was claimed by the
Philippines and Vietnam.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:28.440
And in 2012, it took Scarborough Shoal,

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.960
just 120 nautical miles west

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.420
of the Philippine Island of Luzon.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.150
Then China started to
build on the islands,

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.040
which concerned the US,

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.440
and prompted President Xi Jinping

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.560
to make this assurance in 2015.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.930
- [Interpreter] We are
committed to maintaining

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:48.210
peace and stability in the South China Sea

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:51.870
and China does not intend
to pursue militarization.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.100
- [Narrator] Not long after,

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:56.610
the US says the PRC broke its promise.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:04:00.120
China now has 20 outposts
in the Paracel Islands

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.070
and seven in the Spratlys,

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:05.250
several of which have
aircraft hangers, missiles,

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:09.330
military jamming equipment,
and other advanced systems.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:10.710
Throughout this process,

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:13.590
some US officials expressed concern.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:16.020
They said they repeatedly told the Chinese

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.370
they were making a mistake,

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:20.670
driving countries in the region
closer to the US militarily

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.893
and herding China's ties with Washington.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.080
And in 2016, something critical happened.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.320
The Philippines brought China
to an international tribunal

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.770
over its occupation of
Filipino territories

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:36.870
and the Philippines won.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.720
The Hague said that
China's claims are illegal

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.340
and all the islands it had built

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.190
would not expand its
exclusive economic zone.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:46.170
But China boycotted the tribunal

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:48.273
and refused to recognize the ruling.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:53.580
The US has taken steps to
counter China in two ways;

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.320
boosting its military presence

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.753
and strengthening
diplomatic relationships.

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:02.850
America and the Philippines
have been mutual defense allies

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.900
since 1951, which means if
either countries attacked,

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.003
the other must come to its aid.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:14.790
In 2014, the US and the Philippines

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:18.180
signed the enhanced Defense
Cooperation Agreement.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.220
The EDCA give America access

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.650
to five military bases in the Philippines

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:26.010
where the US can build
infrastructure and rotate troops.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.870
However, the two countries relations

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.090
have teetered over the years.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:33.595
The previous president of the
Philippines, Rodrigo Duterte,

00:05:33.595 --> 00:05:36.450
briefly strengthened
relationships with China,

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:40.170
which in turn weakened the
Philippines' ties to the US.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:43.481
But the shift was
short-lived, and by 2021,

00:05:43.481 --> 00:05:45.780
the Philippines changed course.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:46.613
This year

00:05:46.613 --> 00:05:49.560
EDCA expanded to include four more bases

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:52.320
where the two countries ran
their largest military trails

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.220
in decades.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.120
- If it's an issue for the Philippines

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.729
in terms of international relations,

00:05:58.729 --> 00:06:00.690
it's an issue for the United States

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:03.210
because we're a mutual
defense treaty partner

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:05.100
and we will come to the
aid of the Philippines

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.270
if they're attacked.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:08.820
And I think it's as simple as that.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:11.430
- [Narrator] In response to
this growing cooperation,

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:14.370
China's foreign ministry
spokesperson, Mao Ning,

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.200
said it would escalate tensions

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.350
and endanger peace and
stability in the region.

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.090
- Well, there's a superpower struggle.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:24.330
There's the geopolitical
competition, US and China,

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:28.320
but China is violating our
sovereignty and sovereign rights.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.270
And regardless of there is a competition,

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:32.470
we have an issue with
China in that respect.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.550
- [Narrator] The US
also regularly conducts

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:42.150
freedom of navigation operations
in the South China Sea.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:45.420
FONOPs are meant to challenge
China's claims in the sea

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.240
by demonstrating that the
United States will fly,

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:51.900
sail, and operate wherever
international law allows.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:54.600
The PRC calls these FONOPs illegal.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:57.450
Still, the US has
strengthened its relationships

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.010
with other nearby nations

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:02.550
and encouraged some to run
patrols through the sea as well.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:03.480
In a recent call

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.660
with General Secretary
Nguyen Pho Trong of Vietnam,

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.120
he and Biden discussed how to maintain

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.880
a free and open Indo-Pacific.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.540
China and Vietnam have long
held diplomatic relations

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.140
and Vietnam's economy
relies on this relationship.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.850
But like the Philippines,

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.190
Vietnam has also faced difficulties

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:26.190
operating in its own
exclusive economic zone

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:29.010
due to China's encroachment
and harassment.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:32.220
This gave the US an opportunity
to strengthen its ties

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:35.100
with yet another country
in the South China Sea.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.250
- We greatly value the
relationships we have

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:40.560
with all of these countries in the region.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.300
And there's one constant among all of them

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.700
and that is we respect their sovereignty

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:48.960
and that's where the PRC, I
believe, is missing the mark

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:52.410
because they wanna operate
on their own set of rules

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:54.660
and not respect the sovereignty

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.127
of the other existing
nations in the region.

00:07:57.127 --> 00:07:59.877
(brooding music)

